    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33488" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pallĭŏlātus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		palliolum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>covered with a cloak-cape</i> or <i>hood</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palliolatus novo more praesedit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Claud. 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. 9, 33, 1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tunicae palliolatae,</span>”
				<i>hooded mantles</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vop. Bonos. 15</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Dig. 34, 2, 39</span></i>.</div>
